  'the-1.6': ['Use the order axioms on \\(x>0\\) or \\(-x>0\\) to obtain \\(x^2>0\\), hence \\(1>0\\).', 'Show \\(1/x>0\\) when \\(x>0\\) by ruling out a negative reciprocal.', 'Multiply \\(0<x<y\\) by \\(1/(xy)>0\\) and use \\(-1\\) to get the sign rules.'],
  'the-9.5': ['For every \\(m\\ge N\\), compare the suprema and infima over the two tails.', 'Let \\(m\\to\\infty\\) to get the two comparison inequalities.', 'For the sum, bound its tail supremum by the sum of the two tail suprema and pass to the limit when the sum is defined.'],
  'the-10.3': ['The partial sums \\(S_n=\\sum_{k=1}^n a_k\\) are increasing since \\(a_k\\ge0\\).', 'If the partial sums converge, they are bounded.', 'If the partial sums are bounded, monotone convergence gives a finite limit.'],
  'the-12.2': ['Write the partial sum of the Cauchy product as \\(\\sum_{k=0}^n a_k B_{n-k}\\).', 'Subtract \\(A_nB\\) and fix a split at \\(K\\).', 'The finitely many head terms tend to zero; the tail is bounded by \\(\\sup_m|B_m-B|\\sum_{k>K}|a_k|\\).', 'Make the tail arbitrarily small and use \\(A_nB\\to AB\\).'],
