  'the-14.8': ['If \\(E\\) is unbounded, take \\(f(x)=|x|\\). If \\(E\\) is bounded and noncompact, take \\(f(x)=1/|x-p|\\) for \\(p\\in\\overline E\\setminus E\\).', 'In either case \\(f\\) is continuous and unbounded, while \\(f/(1+f)\\) has supremum \\(1\\) with no maximum.', 'On bounded \\(E\\), any uniformly continuous real function is bounded by a finite cover of small-diameter pieces.', 'Therefore in the bounded case the constructed \\(f\\) is not uniformly continuous.'],
  'the-18.5': ['Surround the finitely many discontinuities by intervals with arbitrarily small total \\(\\alpha\\)-increment.', 'Include their endpoints in a partition; the oscillation on the bad intervals is at most \\(2\\|f\\|_\\infty\\).', 'On the remaining compact pieces use uniform continuity of \\(f\\) and refine to make the oscillations small.', 'Bound \\(U-L\\) by the two contributions and use the integrability criterion.'],
